  "worked_solution": "To find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
